{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /tmp/6c-guard-probes.log\nsed -n '310,345p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\ngit diff --quiet\"","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nFAIL in () (safepoint_harness_test.cljc:1456)\nthe correspondence is injective\nexpected: (= (count names) (count (distinct (vals names))))\n  actual: (not (= 2 1))\n:duplicate-correspondence {:test 0, :pass 0, :fail 1, :error 0}\n\nFAIL in () (safepoint_harness_test.cljc:1586)\ndescriptors equivalent under the correspondence\nexpected: (descriptors-equivalent? (mapv :descriptors roots))\n  actual: (not (descriptors-equivalent? [{:yin/call-in #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :yin/call-in}, :identity :yin/call-in}, :yin/call-out #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :yin/call-out}, :identity :yin/call-out}, :stream-0 #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :stream-0}, :identity :stream-0}} {:yin/call-in #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :yin/call-in}, :identity :yin/call-in}, :yin/call-out #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :yin/call-out}, :identity :yin/call-out}, :stream-0 #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :stream-0}, :identity :stream-0}} {:yin/call-in #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :dao.stream/identity :yin/call-in, :review/extra :different}, :identity :yin/call-in}, :yin/call-out #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :yin/call-out}, :identity :yin/call-out}, :stream-0 #:dao.stream{:outcome :dao.stream/ok, :descriptor #:dao.stream{:type :dao.stream/ringbuffer, :identity :stream-0}, :identity :stream-0}}]))\n:real-descriptor-change {:test 0, :pass 27, :fail 1, :error 0}\n   it, never the cell itself. Not to be confused with `yin.vm.cell`, the\n   general heap box. Vocabulary: UCF §7.5.3, \\\"Terminology\\\".\"\n  [resource]\n  (and (map? resource) (contains? resource :stream-id)))\n\n\n(defn issue-ref\n  \"A reference of `kind` (`:stream-ref`, `:cursor-ref`, or `:cell-ref`) to\n   resource or heap cell `id`, sealed under the task's capability secret.\n   A task composed\n   without a secret cannot issue one: it fails closed rather than issue a\n   reference anyone could forge.\"\n  [state kind id]\n  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)]\n    (when (nil? secret)\n      (fail (str \"This task has no capability secret, so it cannot issue\"\n                 \" a resource reference\")\n            {:reason :no-capability-secret, :kind kind, :id id}))\n    {:type kind, :id id, :seal (seal-of secret kind id)}))\n\n\n(defn authentic-ref?\n  \"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\n   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\n   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\n   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\n   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\"\n  [state kind ref]\n  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\n        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\n    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\n      (let [heap (:heap state)]\n        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n                      (= kind (:type ref))\n                      (contains? heap id)\n                      (= (:seal ref) (:seal (get heap id))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
