{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > /tmp/6c-review-draft.md <<'EOF'\n# Slice 6c fix-round-1 re-review — gpt-6.1-sol\n\nReviewed \"'`srvm-phase6c`, HEAD `dc545aaa`, `git diff 47ddb1d9..HEAD`, against F1–F6 and the Architect'\"'s R1–R6. This is an independent mutation review. Only this findings artifact is retained in the worktree; every temporary source/test mutant was restored.\n\nThe requested JVM suites and lint pass. The implemented refusals behave correctly in the probes, but native layout tests still depend on global projection history, and four independently applied mutants survive both test tiers.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Priority | Location | Finding / required action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N1 | P2 | \"'`layout_test.cljc:108–114, 199–203, 250, 280–287, 350–363`; harness `kernel-space:138–145` | **R1'\"'s scoping fix is incomplete.** Law 4 and law 5 use \"'`scoped`, but these native layout fixtures still use the global index. Projecting an unrelated alpha-equivalent higher-order fixture makes `closures-round-trip` throw `:yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image`. Scope each independent world'\"'s construction and all its native layout lookups, including the remaining harness refusal helpers, with \"'`h/scoped`; keep intentional global-contamination tests explicit. Test-unique syntax is not structural isolation. |\n| N2 | P2 | harness `injective:1453–1457`, `canonical-equality:1586`, `law-4-controls:1623–1628` | **The injectivity and descriptor guards can both be removed without failing either tier.** The descriptor negative control calls `descriptors-equivalent?` on manually altered maps; it does not prove that the law-4 comparison invokes that guard. All normal name maps are injective, so removing that assertion also passes. Add a duplicate-correspondence negative control and a real one-lane descriptor change through the law-4 comparison, observing the failed assertion/refusal. Both guard-removal mutants must be killed. |\n| N3 | P2 | `layout.cljc:877–897`; `layout_test.cljc:534–557` | **The recursive free-environment refusal is unprotected.** Changing `row-procedure` to inspect only the top-level value survives quick and slow. Baseline correctly refuses a closure nested in guest vector/map values, and that raw nested value would otherwise bypass native conversion just as F1'\"'s top-level closure did. Add nested closure/continuation fixtures in both directions, pin path/key and zero attaches/serves, with admitted primitive and authentic cursor controls. |\n| N4 | P3 | \"'`layout.cljc:905–913`; `layout_test.cljc:499–506` | **Receiver-specific image derivation is not pinned.** Swapping the stack and register image hash functions survives both tiers. The alpha fixture collides under both, and the test checks A membership but not `:yin.k/image`. Baseline uses the correct functions. Assert the refusal'\"'s image is exactly \"'`dcode/image-hash` of `(:image (derive/stack-image v))` or `rcode/register-hash` of `derive/register-image v` for the receiver, plus a noncollision when only one of the pair is carried. |\n\nN2–N4 are mutation/coverage findings, not claims that baseline currently omits those checks.\n\n### Reproduction for N1 (unmodified code)\n\nAfter requiring the layout test, harness and `clojure.walk`:\n\n```clojure\n(let [ast (second (second lt/closure-programs))\n      renamed (walk/postwalk #(if (= % '\"'x) 'review-y %) ast)]\n  (h/project (h/with-stream (h/with-cat renamed)))\n  (clojure.test/test-vars [#'lt/closures-round-trip]))\n\"'```\n\nResult: **1 test, 10 passes, 0 failures, 1 error**. The error is `:yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image`, native image `95c900adc44f2c35e5b97835db32836de1cebf55870956edd3275041958026e9`, through `canonical-closure` → `image-pc` → `image-segment`. Neither source nor test is mutated. The different binder contributes an unrelated A to the global index but the same native image as the fixture.\n\n## F1–F6 / rulings disposition\n\n| Previous finding | Disposition |\n|---|---|\n| F1 / R3 | **Original bug addressed by the ruled native-domain refusal**, rather than conversion. The independent `(then (next-of c) (f \"B\"))` closure fixture passes on the reference lane and through its carrier; both native lowers refuse `:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value`, path `[:free-env f]`, before attach; both native lifts refuse `:yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value`, key `f`, before serve. Nested baseline behavior is correct, but protection remains N3. |\n| F2 / R1 | **Collision refusal fixed; scoping only partially fixed (N1).** Independent identity probes show `(fn [x] x)` and `(fn [y] y)` have different A and equal H/R. Both native lift/lower refusals pin their required statuses and zero serves/attaches. Reference-lane lowering/relifting/continuation with both closures answers `\"B\"`. Receiver image derivation is correct but unprotected (N4). |\n| F3 / R2 | The declared shared-fragment counts pass: quick law 4/5 **16/92**, slow **61/350**, with all three native/reference lanes and the admitted ordered pairs. **Q1 and Q2 remain owner decisions. They do not hold this re-review**, as instructed. This report does not treat Q1 as accepted or claim the original 89/534 native gate is fulfilled. |\n| F4 / R4 | **Partially closed.** Reference-only and two-lane mutants are killed; replacing positions by `:constant` is killed; saved and lexical value controls change the compared roots. Three-lane assertions are non-vacuous. Baseline detects a real descriptor change and a duplicate correspondence, but the shipped tests do not protect those guards (N2). |\n| F5 / R5 | **Closed.** `virt` implements the one-live-preimage, sole-named-dead-preimage diagnostic fallback and `:yin.k/non-portable :register-layout` refusal on ambiguity. The 38 ambiguous-dead-slot fixtures pin pc/register/status/kind; first-preimage selection is killed with 76 failures. Unique-dead `:window-extra` and dropped-live `:window-missing` controls remain green. |\n| F6 / R6 | **Closed.** The unused `rvm` require is gone; four changed files lint with 0 errors and 0 warnings. |\n\nR6'\"'s D4 cases pass for primitive payloads in a saved window, lexical binding, closure capture and nested guest collection: register refusal \"'`:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers`, path and zero attaches, with stack continuation controls. Free-environment primitives remain admitted; the restriction is not a general primitive carrier ban. The two allowlist entries name the exact `canonical-task`/`kernel-task` `assoc` sites and explain the already-validated store keys as ruled. An entry with the wrong site is killed by the audit.\n\nThe fix diff changes no design document. Its comments cite R2'\"'s proposed §5.3 wording; the Architect's mechanical design pass and owner answers are still separate integration work. The status/kind distinctions above agree with the rulings: receiver limitations are \"'`unsupported`, native lift ambiguity/free procedures and ambiguous inverse layouts are `non-portable`. No first-A/preimage choice was introduced.\n\n## Independent baseline probes\n\n- **Collision domain:** a valid reference task built after projecting both alpha-equivalent closures, with both store names pointing to the first closure, carries only that A plus the parked program (2 code entries). It lowers successfully to stack and register, remains blocked, and attaches exactly one stream. Merely projecting the uncarried second A does not create a receiver collision. The task carrying both A continues through the reference lane and answers `\"B\"`.\n- **Free-environment scope:** direct decoded-task probes yield `:free-env-value` at `[:free-env f 0 1]` for a closure in a vector containing a map, on both native receivers; primitive, cursor-reference and plain-data values produce no free-env defect. Native-source probes with a nested guest map/vector closure refuse before any serve, while a primitive, the actual wait'\"'s cursor reference and data lift successfully (one served stream each). These scope probes supplement, rather than replace, full transported fixture tests requested in N3.\n- **Descriptor/injectivity controls:** baseline \"'`h/injective` on `{:id1 :same :id2 :same}` records exactly one failed assertion. Redefining the real `logical-descriptors` output on only the register lane to add `:review/extra :different` and running `canonical-equality` on row 1 records exactly one failed descriptor assertion (27 passes, 0 errors). Baseline is correct; deleting its guard survives the repository suites because these decisive inputs are absent there.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll tests were foreground commands (no background shell jobs), with output retained under `/tmp`.\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\nclojure -M:test -i :slow -n yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\nclojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj\n```\n\n| Baseline | Tests | Assertions | Failures | Errors |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Requested quick tier | 66 | 4,274 | 0 | 0 |\n| Requested slow tier | 4 | 3,517 | 0 | 0 |\n| Kondo | — | — | 0 errors | 0 warnings |\n\n### Own mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied to one file copied with `shutil.copy2` to `/tmp` first. After each quick/slow run the file was restored with `copy2`, checked with `diff -q` against its backup and `git diff --quiet -- <file>`. Final tracked-worktree diff is clean. Quick runs used layout-test, safepoint-harness-test and store-write-audit-test: **37 tests**. All four quick survivors were rerun independently in the same namespaces'\"' slow tier: **3 tests**. Baseline slow there has 3,509 assertions; the required four-namespace command also includes rows-test.\n\n| Mutant | Quick result | Slow result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Drop \"'`image-collision` clause | Killed: 6 failures, 0 errors | Not needed |\n| Stack uses register hash/derivation; register uses stack hash/derivation | **Survives: 3,821 assertions** | **Survives: 3,509 assertions** |\n| Free-env check only top-level (`row-procedure` stops at guest collections) | **Survives: 3,821 assertions** | **Survives: 3,509 assertions** |\n| `kernel-space` ignores `*projected*` | Killed: 2 failures, 2 errors | Not needed |\n| Law 4 compares only first two lanes | Killed: 36 failures, 1 error | Not needed |\n| Law 4 compares only reference lane (old M11) | Killed: 37 failures, 3 errors | Not needed |\n| Renamed positions become `:constant` (old M12) | Killed: 1 failure, 0 errors | Not needed |\n| Remove injectivity assertion | **Survives: 3,608 assertions** | **Survives: 2,777 assertions** |\n| Remove law-4 descriptor-equivalence assertion | **Survives: 3,804 assertions** | **Survives: 3,448 assertions** |\n| `virt` returns first live/named preimage (old M9) | Killed: 76 failures, 0 errors | Not needed |\n| Audit allowlist uses `kernel-task-WRONG` site | Killed: 1 failure, 0 errors | Not needed |\n\nThe top-level-only mutant targets the receiver check; the source still walks nested guest collections. The inverse mutant'\"'s exercised ambiguous cases are the dead/named branch, as intended by R5; allocator live injectivity prevents the live branch from becoming ambiguous on valid fixtures.\n\n## Scanner / process-test attribution\n\nSCAN_RESULT_PENDING\n\nNode and Dart acceptance lanes were not run; the prompt requests JVM review. The missing Node dependency is not counted as a layout-test failure.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
